<title>RUSSIA: Russia institute sees 96 gold output down.</title>
<headline>Russia institute sees 96 gold output down.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1996-08-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russian gold output will fall to 101.3 tonnes this year from 110.8 tonnes in 1995, the government's Centre for Economic Trends said.</p>
<p>The nine percent fall in output this year will follow a 12 percent drop in 1995, it said in a set of forecasts in the government bulletin published on Tuesday.</p>
<p>-- Jonathan Lynn, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
